Nvidia today <a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director">announced</a> that its board of directors has voted unanimously to reinstate Jensen Huang as President and CEO of the company effective immediately.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Nvidia-16x9-1.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078927" /><br/>
Huang had <a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-ceo-transition">resigned</a> on November 12, after it was reported that he had extramarital affairs.<br/>
<br/>
Nvidia's board voted unanimously to reinstate Huang following "a series of discussions and meetings" with him, after which the board was satisfied with respect to his "candor and ability to lead" the company. The board received input from "senior levels of the U.S. government" and is confident that Huang "poses no national security risk."<br/>
<br/>
"The Board believes Jensen is the right person to lead NVIDIA, and that his reinstatement is in the best interests of our stockholders, employees, partners and customers," said Nvidia's chairman Harvey C. Jones. "We have every confidence in Jensen and look forward to working with him as he resumes his leadership of the Company."<br/>
<br/>
Speaking on a November 17 earnings call, Jones said Nvidia's board did not intend to reinstate Huang, so the company has reversed course.<br/>
<br/>
